course: dictionary
lesson: 14583
title: Planned
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Planned is the past form of the verb plan. To plan something is to decide in advance what you will do and how you will do it. «We planned our trip to the zoo for weeks.» The word tells you the trip was thought about before it happened.
explain: Planned can also be an adjective, describing something that has been arranged beforehand. «The fire drill was planned, so everyone knew where to go.» Nobody was surprised, because the drill had been arranged in advance.
explain: Look at the words around planned for clues. Words like ahead, carefully and for often show that something was thought about first. «Ben planned ahead and packed his bag the night before.» Ahead tells you Ben got ready early.
fact: Planned means decided in advance what to do and how.
fact: A planned thing has been arranged before it happens.
fact: «Planned ahead» means you thought about the future and got ready early.
fact: Plan is the base word: plan, plans, planning, planned.
exercise: «We planned our trip to the zoo for weeks.» What does planned mean here? | Lost on the way | Ran away quickly | *Decided in advance what to do | Forgotten completely
exercise: «The science test was planned so that only one thing changed.» What does a planned test mean? | *A test that was arranged in advance | A test with no rules | A test made up on the spot | A test nobody could finish
exercise: Nadia says planned means random. Why is she wrong? | Planned is a longer word than random | *Planned means arranged in advance, the opposite of random | Planned means random, so she is right | Planned means happy
test: «The fire drill was carefully planned by the teacher.» What does carefully planned suggest? | Forgotten halfway through | *Thought about and arranged well beforehand | Done in a rush at the last minute | Done by accident
test: «Ben planned ahead and packed his bag the night before.» What does planned ahead mean? | *Thought about and got ready early | Walked slowly behind | Shouted for help | Lost his way
exam: «The planned picnic was cancelled because of the rain.» What does planned tell you about the picnic? | It was about the weather | *It was arranged before it was due to happen | It was a secret from everyone | It happened by surprise
